==Trivia==
* The player can also teleport to the ship without reaching Lv. 1000 through the use of [[Portal]]'s {{Ability|Portal|C}}. If the player enters the ship without reaching Lv. 1000, they still will be able to talk to the [[NPCs]]. However, the [[Cursed Captain]] will not drop the [[Hellfire Torch]], and the player will not be able to accept any quests (because of the level requirement).
** Another way to access this area is by going to the docks at the [[Kingdom of Rose]], flying forward until the ship comes into view, and then glitching inside using [[Flash Step]]. However, this method is somewhat difficult due to the kill barriers which deal more damage than touching [[water]] with a fruit equipped or [[lava]] without [[Tiger]] or [[Magma]], surrounding the area. Alternatively, the player can simply die when the 'Cursed Ship' message and music appear, which will teleport them inside if below level 1000.
* Jumping to the roof of the Cursed Ship will cause the head of the player to glitch outside and damage them.
* It is possible to get both the [[Red Spikey Coat|Red]] and [[Blue Spikey Coat]] at the same time from the [[Cursed Captain]].
* The [[Barista Cousin]] can be found underneath the right staircase when entering from outside.
* The [[Ship Steward]]s used to have a bloody scratch on their chest, but it was later removed.
* When the player is in the ship during the night, using unawakened [[Buddha]]'s transformation will help them see a little better in the dark.
* If the player were to open up the compass and go towards the box, the compass' arrow would break after a while, and it will change (not to the player's current quest giver) but directly to the Cursed Ship's area location.
* It is roughly 25 seconds faster(per 3 lvl's) to grind the [[Ship Deckhand]]'s rather than the [[Ship Engineer]]'s.
* [[Quake]]'s {{Ability|Quake|V}} or {{Ability|Quake|V|1}} move can hit all the enemies in the ship, making it great for auto-farming without exploits if you use an auto-clicker.
* Since the Cursed Ship gets very dark at night, turning on [[Fast Mode|fast mode]] can make the area brighter if the player does not use [[Buddha]].
* The Cursed Ship is actually a gear of "Ghost Ship" Item. The gear ID of this ship is 155662051.
* The engine in the engine room has [[Destructible Physics]].  
* Despite there being no official way to fish at the Cursed Ship, players have found a way to [[Flash Step|flashstep]] out onto a part of the ship's exterior, one which is close to the water's surface and lacks the damaging floor.
* Due to it being mostly empty, it’s one of the better locations to AFK levels.
* The three [[Shop]] [[NPCs]] aboard the ship have unique themes for their names.
** [[El Admin|El Admin's]] name likely is a joke, since admins are often asked for strong things, hence he sells the [[Midnight Blade]], a strong sword.
** [[El Rodolfo|El Rodolfo's]] name resembles one commonly used for old timey gun slingers, hence he sells the [[Bizarre Revolver]].
** [[El Perro|El Perro's]] name in Spanish for 'dog', a reference to him selling the [[Ghoul Mask]].
